{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_packing_decision_flowcharts_document", "label": "Box Agriculture: packing decisions and rule changes", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DECISION_FLOWCHARTS.md", "source_location": "L1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_packing_decision_flowcharts_forward_packing_lifecycle", "label": "Forward packing lifecycle", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DECISION_FLOWCHARTS.md", "source_location": "L28", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Normal lifecycle: upload \u2192 parse \u2192 split and validate \u2192 consolidate purchasing \u2192 confirm procurement \u2192 Handoff 01 \u2192 design packing \u2192 floor packing \u2192 lock final pack \u2192 Handoff 02. Normal transitions move forward one stage. Template fast-track is a separate shortcut. ## 2. Upload, validate, and create customer orders"}, {"id": "docs_packing_decision_flowcharts_deterministic_box_heuristic", "label": "Deterministic box heuristic", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DECISION_FLOWCHARTS.md", "source_location": "L185", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Usable volume is catalogue volume \u00d7 0.92. This is a deterministic weight-and-volume heuristic, not a 3D layout or guaranteed minimum-box solution. There is no physical bottom/top placement decision. ## 7. Add, edit, substitute, or remove a packed item"}, {"id": "docs_packing_decision_flowcharts_usable_volume_allowance", "label": "Usable-volume allowance", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DECISION_FLOWCHARTS.md", "source_location": "L185", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Usable volume is catalogue volume \u00d7 0.92. This is a deterministic weight-and-volume heuristic, not a 3D layout or guaranteed minimum-box solution. There is no physical bottom/top placement decision. ## 7. Add, edit, substitute, or remove a packed item"}, {"id": "docs_packing_decision_flowcharts_historical_live_rule_coupling", "label": "Historical live-rule coupling", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DECISION_FLOWCHARTS.md", "source_location": "L319", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Handoff 01 captures some product rules, but the current packing service reads live product records rather than using that saved rule snapshot. A master-data change after Handoff 01 can therefore alter subsequent design behavior without altering the earlier handoff. Existing boxes store their route; a customer route edit does not automatically update it. Locked boxes reference live products/catalogues rather than a fully versioned rule set. ### Expected effect on a newly generated plan"}, {"id": "docs_packing_decision_flowcharts_historical_nga_exception", "label": "Historical NGA exception", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DECISION_FLOWCHARTS.md", "source_location": "L157", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "EL products with missing botanical family use their product ID as the family fallback. OTHER products are isolated by product ID on every route. Product type and weight class come from master data; the optimizer does not derive them from names or pack weight. NGA means an exact route match: `GROUP NGA` does not trigger the exception. No certificate or destination exemption is checked here. ## 6. Select a box for every whole pack"}, {"id": "docs_packing_decision_flowcharts_floor_constraint_validation", "label": "Floor constraint validation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DECISION_FLOWCHARTS.md", "source_location": "L249", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Current floor validation checks material, temperature, staff-selected EL rules, product grouping, weight class, safe capacity and estimated volume for moves, transfers and box changes. Custom dimensions cannot bypass the workbook catalogue."}, {"id": "docs_packing_decision_flowcharts_template_fast_track_shortcut", "label": "Template fast-track shortcut", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DECISION_FLOWCHARTS.md", "source_location": "L294", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This shortcut skips normal procurement/floor weighing and the automatic grouping and volume checks. Zero confirmed values can fall back to ordered values because the implementation uses truthy fallback expressions. Group fast-track runs this operation separately for each selected customer order; it does not combine customers into a box. ## 11. What actually happens when rules change"}, {"id": "docs_packing_decision_flowcharts_proposed_rule_change_handling", "label": "Proposed rule-change handling", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DECISION_FLOWCHARTS.md", "source_location": "L338", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "## 12. Recommended rule-change handling \u2014 not implemented ```mermaid flowchart TD"}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_packing_decision_flowcharts_document", "target": "docs_packing_decision_flowcharts_forward_packing_lifecycle", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DECISION_FLOWCHARTS.md", "source_location": "L28", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_packing_decision_flowcharts_document", "target": "docs_packing_decision_flowcharts_deterministic_box_heuristic", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/PACKING_DECISION_FLOWCHARTS.md", "source_location": "L185", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_packing_decision_flowcharts_document", "target"